## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical IAM policy construction tying S3 prefixes to service identities, a common beginner task for real-world isolation.

## Key Concepts
- IAM policies and bucket policies
- s3:prefix and path-based access control
- Least privilege and revocation testing
- Trust policy basics for role assumption

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/*"]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus",
        "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/logs/${serviceName}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"s3:prefix": "logs/${serviceName}/"}
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:GetObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::logs-campus/logs/*"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce encryption at rest for these objects?
- How would you audit access attempts and detect violations?
- How would you handle new services joining without updating policies frequently?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses design for fair throughput, scalability, and auditable enforcement in a shared data lake.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant quotas; token bucket; API Gateway usage plans; DynamoDB; Lambda; S3 prefixes; CloudWatch; Kinesis Firehose; testing at scale.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, burst) {
    this.rate = rate; // tokens per second
    this.burst = burst;
    this.tokens = burst;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.burst, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test multi-tenant fairness under bursty conditions and validate SLA guarantees?
- What changes if large tenants typically spike during business hours?
